<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">1. The above consolidated financial results of the Company, its subsidiaries, (together 'Group ) and its Associate were reviewed by the Audit Committee and approved by the Board of Directors in its meeting held on August 08, 2020. The Consolidated Financial Results are prepared in accordance with the Indian Accounting Standards (Ind-AS) as prescribed under Section 133 of the Companies Act, 2013 read with the relevant rules issued thereunder. The Statutory audtiors have carried out an limited review of the above results and have expressed an unqualified opinion.  n  n2.  Employee benefits expense includes cost towards the proportionate fair value of the stock options granted to various employees, amortised over the graded vesting period ('ESOP Cost ). Such ESOP Cost for the quarter includes Rs.0.12 Mln. USD 0.00 (Rs.5.47 Mlm. USD 0.08 Mln.). Other expenses for  nthe quarter includes foreign exchange fluctuation gain of Rs.58.60 Mlm. USD 0.78 Mln.(loss of Rs.25.44 Mln. USD 0.37 Mlm.) and bad debts / provision for doubtful debts &amp; advances of Rs.119.52 Mln. USD 1.60 Mln (Rs.85.04 Mlm. USD 1.23 Mlm.).  n  n3.During the quarter, the Company had allotted a total of 1,752 equity shares of Rs.10/- each under the Employees Stock Option Schemes of the Company on various dates. Accordingly, as at the date, the paid up capital of the Company increased to Rs.306.40 Mln. USD 6.05 Mlm. from Rs.306.39 Mln. USD 6.05 Mm. as at March 31, 2020.  n  n4. Estimation of uncertainties relating to the Global Pandemic COVID-19'):  nThe Group has, based on the information available, taken into account the possible impacts of COVID-19, including on the carrying amounts of financial and non-financial assets and as per the current assessment of the Group, there is no material impact in respect of these in the preparation of the unaudited quarterly consolidated financial results ('the Statement'). However, the impact of COVID-19 on the Statement may differ from that  nestimated as at the date of approval of the Statement and the Group will continue to monitor the uncertainties caused by COVID-19 to assess the impact on our future economic conditions.  n  n5. The Group has only one operating segment-viz., Software Solutions &amp; Services.  n  n6.  Figures for the previous period(s) have been regrouped / restated wherever necessary to make them comparable with the figures for the current period(s). Figures for the quarter ended March 31, 2020 are the balancing figures between audited figures in respect of the financial year ended March 31, 2020 and published year to date figures up to the third quarter ended December 31, 2019.</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
